  "title": "North Korea's Missile Launch and U.S. Military Drills Reduction",
  "summary": "North Korea launches a suspected ballistic missile toward the sea, citing a U.S. military order to scale back drills with South Korea, while South Korea's military reported a missile launch from the region of Pyongyang. The U.S. and South Korea are seen as responding to North Korea's evolving battlefield tactics.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "North Korea launched about 10 short-range ballistic missiles toward the sea on Thursday, according to South Korean military reports.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. military ordered the Pentagon to scale back U.S.-South Korea joint military drills, citing a'very good relationship' with North Korea.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "North Korea's missile launch coincided with a U.S. decision to reduce drills with South Korea, which was seen as a counter to North Korea's evolving strategy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
